PASS conjugation by every projective normalizer of <S> preserves epsilon_2 (16 normalizers)
== class-two identities (E.65 'integral sign') ==
PASS [x,y] = x y x^{-1} y^{-1} is the central e13 in the Heisenberg model
PASS E.65.11: theta(h)^{-1} h = [x,y]^{rho^2 + 2d}
PASS [y,z] = [x,y] and [z,x] = [x,y] in class two (z = (xy)^{-1})
PASS x^{-rho} y^{-rho} x^{rho} y^{rho} = [x,y]^{rho^2}
== Marin-type intertwiner (E.65.15) ==
PASS (2,1) entry of NMN - MNM is -c(1 + lambda c)
PASS the second family [[1-u, lambda u^2],[-1/lambda, 1+u]] satisfies the braid relation with U^lambda and det 1
PASS with c = -1/lambda the relation forces b = lambda (a-1)^2
PASS with c = 0 and det 1, a = d = 1 (abelian pair)
PASS V U V^{-1} = U^lambda and V L V^{-1} = second matrix
PASS E.64.25: AU - UA = [[-c, a-d],[0, c]] and AL - LA = [[-b, 0],[a-d, b]]
PASS product of normalized intertwiners is normalized: [[l1,t1],[0,1]][[l2,t2],[0,1]] = [[l1 l2, l1 t2 + t1],[0,1]]
PASS a shear [[1,m],[0,1]] conjugates S to [[-m, 1+m^2],[-1, m]] (so +-S forces m = 0 mod 12)
PASS conjugate of unipotent shear by normalized intertwiner: [[l,t],[0,1]][[1,k],[0,1]][[l,t],[0,1]]^{-1} = [[1,l k],[0,1]]
